{
    "_id": "irish-coffee",
    "name": "Irish Coffee",
    "instructions": "1. Warm black coffee is poured into a pre-heated Irish coffee glass.\n2. Whiskey and at least one teaspoon of sugar is added and stirred until dissolved.\n3. Fresh thick chilled cream is carefully poured over the back of a spoon held just above the surface of the coffee.\n4. The layer of cream will float on the coffee without mixing.\n5. Plain sugar can be replaced with sugar syrup",
